     A                                  1 14'REQUISITION INQUIRY/APPROVAL HELP'
     A                                  1 48'SCREEN'
     A                                  1 61'2 OF 6'
     A                                  4  1'EXCLUDE OPTIONS'
     A                                  5  1'---------------'
     A                                  6  1'These options let you see subsets'
     A                                  6 35'of the data requested in the selec-
     A                                      tion'
     A                                  7  1'options.  Example:  if looking for'
     A                                  7 36'all reqs for WO 1086H, you could l-
     A                                      ook at'
     A                                  8  1'non-coded items only.  These optio-
     A                                      ns are also used for requisition ap-
     A                                      proval:'
     A                                  9  1'to select only those reqs for an a-
     A                                      pprover that have not already been'
     A                                  9 70'approved.'
     A                                 10  1'Note: you may exclude multiple ite-
     A                                      ms, but remember that it is possibl-
     A                                      e to'
     A                                 11  1'exclude ALL reqs, and thus the pro-
     A                                      gram will not bring up anything on'
     A                                 11 70'the'
     A                                 12  1'inquiry.  The program will not che-
     A                                      ck for this.  Example:  show all re-
     A                                      qs for'
     A                                 13  1'corporate code 4440011, exclude co-
     A                                      ded storeroom.'
     A                                 15  1'Three of the exclude options have'
     A                                 15 35'to do with the STATUS of the requi-
     A                                      sition.'
     A                                 16  1'There are 3 statuses:'
     A                                 18  3'1.  Awaiting approvals (unapproved-
     A                                      ).  These reqs have not yet gone to'
     A                                 19  7'purchasing.'
     A                                 20  3'2.  In purchasing.  These reqs hav-
     A                                      e been approved, but not yet assign-
     A                                      ed to'
     A                                 21  7'a PO.'
     A                                 22  3'3.  On Purchase Order.  These reqs'
     A                                 22 38'have been assigned to a PO.'
     A            COMMANDLN1    79A  B 24  1DFTVAL('F1-PREV F2-NEXT            -
     A                                                                         -
     A                                                       ')
     A                                      DSPATR(PR)
     A  98                                  OVRDTA
     A  99        MESSAGELN1    79   M
     A  99                                  OVRDTA
